Wilson, and Peter Ackerman.

12
00:42:15,652 --> 00:42:21,652
Produced by Blue Sky Studios as its first feature film, it features an ensemble voice
cast, including Ray Romano, John Leguizamo, Denis Leary and Jack Black.

13
00:45:46,956 --> 00:45:52,956
Set during the days of the Pleistocene ice age, the film centers around Manny, a no-nonsense woolly mammoth, Sid, a loudmouthed
ground sloth, and Diego, a sardonic smilodon, who come across a human baby and work together to return it to its tribe.

14
00:49:18,260 --> 00:49:24,260
Ice Age was originally conceived by Fox Animation Studios as a traditionally animated film, but became a full-length CGI
film from Blue Sky, which had been transformed from a visual effects house to a computer animation studio.

15
00:52:49,565 --> 00:52:55,565
Focus shifted from making an action-adventure drama film to a more comedy-oriented one, and
several writers, including Berg and Ackerman, were brought on to lighten the tone.

16
00:56:20,869 --> 00:56:26,869
David Newman composed and conducted the film's musical score.

17
00:59:52,173 --> 00:59:58,173
Ice Age was released in the United States on March 15, 2002 by 20th Century Fox.

18
01:03:23,478 --> 01:03:29,478
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and was a box office success, grossing $383 million,
and becoming the eighth highest-grossing film and the highest-grossing animated film of 2002.

19
01:06:54,782 --> 01:07:00,782
It was nominated at the 75th Academy Awards for Best Animated Feature.

20
